@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Introduction to Monitoring in DevOps";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Explore the significance of monitoring in DevOps and how it ensures system reliability and performance.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Monitoring in DevOps?</h2>
        <p>
            Monitoring in DevOps refers to the continuous observation and tracking of system performance, application health, and infrastructure status.
            It plays a critical role in identifying performance bottlenecks, troubleshooting issues, and ensuring high availability.
        </p>
        <p>
            DevOps monitoring tools collect metrics, logs, and alerts to provide real-time insights into system behavior, enabling proactive issue resolution.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/devops-monitoring.jpg" alt="DevOps Monitoring Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Monitoring helps in early detection of issues, ensuring system stability.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of Monitoring in DevOps -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Key Benefits of Monitoring</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Early Issue Detection:</strong> Detect problems before they affect users.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Improved Performance:</strong> Optimize application and system performance.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enhanced Security:</strong> Identify security threats and vulnerabilities in real-time.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Better Incident Response:</strong> Enable faster troubleshooting and root cause analysis.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Data-Driven Decision Making:</strong> Use analytics to improve business processes.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/monitoring-benefits.jpg" alt="Benefits of Monitoring in DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Effective monitoring ensures high system availability and reliability.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Types of Monitoring in DevOps -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Types of Monitoring</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Infrastructure Monitoring:</strong> Tracks CPU, memory, network, and server health.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Application Performance Monitoring (APM):</strong> Observes application response times and errors.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Log Monitoring:</strong> Analyzes system logs to detect anomalies and security threats.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Security Monitoring:</strong> Ensures compliance and detects suspicious activities.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>User Experience Monitoring:</strong> Monitors real-user interactions and application usability.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/monitoring-types.jpg" alt="Types of Monitoring in DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Various monitoring approaches help maintain a stable and secure system.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for DevOps Monitoring</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Implement Real-Time Alerts:</strong> Ensure quick response to system failures.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Centralized Logging:</strong> Aggregate logs for better visibility.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Automate Monitoring:</strong> Set up automated checks to reduce manual efforts.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Correlate Metrics & Logs:</strong> Link performance metrics with logs for deeper insights.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Regularly Review Monitoring Data:</strong> Use collected data to refine and optimize system performance.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/best-practices-monitoring.jpg" alt="Best Practices for DevOps Monitoring" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices enhances the effectiveness of monitoring strategies.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Monitoring is an essential component of DevOps, enabling teams to maintain high availability, security, and performance.
            By implementing real-time monitoring tools and best practices, organizations can proactively address issues and deliver superior user experiences.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion-monitoring.jpg" alt="DevOps Monitoring Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Monitoring ensures seamless operations and enhanced system reliability.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>